可以通过 `device.token.rotate` 和 `device.token.revoke` 轮换/撤销（需要 `operator.pairing` 作用域）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:206:- 所有 WS 客户端在 `connect` 期间必须包含 `device` 身份（operator + node）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/troubleshooting.md:235:- 你将 `gateway.bind` 设置为非本地回环模式（`lan`/`tailnet`/`custom`，或本地回环不可用时的 `auto`）但没有配置认证。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/troubleshooting.md:241:- 修复：在该机器上启动 Tailscale（或将 `gateway.bind` 改为 `loopback`/`lan`）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/nodes/index.md:73:如果 Gateway 网关绑定到 loopback（`gateway.bind=loopback`，本地模式下的默认值），\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/start/wizard.md:199:  --gateway-bind loopback \\\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/start/wizard.md:215:  --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/start/wizard.md:226:  --gateway-bind loopback"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":111,"aggregated":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:749:- `config: true` enables `/config` (reads/writes `openclaw.json`). For gateway `chat.send` clients, persistent `/config set|unset` writes also require `operator.admin`; read-only `/config show` stays available to normal write-scoped operator clients.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:1977:- Per-subagent tool policy: `tools.subagents.tools.allow` / `tools.subagents.tools.deny`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2441:    trustedProxies: [\"10.0.0.1\"],\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2467:- **Legacy bind aliases**: use bind mode values in `gateway.bind` (`auto`, `loopback`, `lan`, `tailnet`, `custom`), not host aliases (`0.0.0.0`, `127.0.0.1`, `localhost`, `::`, `::1`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2472:- `gateway.auth.mode: \"trusted-proxy\"`: delegate auth to an identity-aware reverse proxy and trust identity headers from `gateway.trustedProxies` (see [Trusted Proxy Auth](/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth)).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2490:- `trustedProxies`: reverse proxy IPs that terminate TLS. Only list proxies you control.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:2626:- Local-only: keep `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"` (default).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/openai-http-api.md:33:Treat this endpoint as a **full operator-access** surface for the gateway instance.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/openai-http-api.md:36:- A valid Gateway token/password for this endpoint should be treated like an owner/operator credential.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/openai-http-api.md:37:- Requests run through the same control-plane agent path as trusted operator actions.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/openai-http-api.md:38:- There is no separate non-owner/per-user tool boundary on this endpoint; once a caller passes Gateway auth here, OpenClaw treats that caller as a trusted operator for this gateway.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/bonjour.md:76:- Set `gateway.bind: \"tailnet\"` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/bonjour.md:169:- `gateway.bind` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` controls the Gateway bind mode.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated.md:58:- **Global/per-agent tool policy**: `tools.allow`/`tools.deny` and `agents.list[].tools.allow`/`agents.list[].tools.deny`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated.md:59:- **Provider tool policy**: `tools.byProvider[provider].allow/deny` and `agents.list[].tools.byProvider[provider].allow/deny`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated.md:60:- **Sandbox tool policy** (only applies when sandboxed): `tools.sandbox.tools.allow`/`tools.sandbox.tools.deny` and `agents.list[].tools.sandbox.tools.*`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated.md:117:### “Tool X blocked by sandbox tool policy”\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration.md:267:    3. Pair the iOS app to the gateway and let both node and operator sessions connect.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration.md:354:    - For hook-driven agents, prefer strong modern model tiers and strict tool policy (for example messaging-only plus sandboxing where possible).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/gateway-lock.md:21:- The gateway binds the WebSocket listener (default `ws://127.0.0.1:18789`) immediately on startup using an exclusive TCP listener.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/tailscale.md:106:- `gateway.bind: \"tailnet\"` is a direct Tailnet bind (no HTTPS, no Serve/Funnel).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/tailscale.md:107:- `gateway.bind: \"auto\"` prefers loopback; use `tailnet` if you want Tailnet-only.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/tailscale.md:117:Avoid Funnel for browser control; treat node pairing like operator access.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/discovery.md:22:- **Gateway WS (control plane)**: the WebSocket endpoint on `127.0.0.1:18789` by default; can be bound to LAN/tailnet via `gateway.bind`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/discovery.md:81:- `gateway.bind` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` controls the Gateway bind mode.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/openresponses-http-api.md:26:- treat the endpoint as full operator access for the gateway instance\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/secrets.md:367:Default operator flow:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/bridge-protocol.md:15:If you are building an operator or node client, use the\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandboxing.md:115:- See [Sandbox vs Tool Policy vs Elevated](/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated) for how binds interact with tool policy and elevated exec.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandboxing.md:225:`exec`, use tool policy deny (see [Sandbox vs Tool Policy vs Elevated](/gateway/sandbox-vs-tool-policy-vs-elevated)).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandboxing.md:229:- Use `openclaw sandbox explain` to inspect effective sandbox mode, tool policy, and fix-it config keys.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/sandboxing.md:236:`agents.list[].sandbox` and `agents.list[].tools` (plus `agents.list[].tools.sandbox.tools` for sandbox tool policy).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:11:> **Personal assistant trust model:** this guidance assumes one trusted operator boundary per gateway (single-user/personal assistant model).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:17:OpenClaw security guidance assumes a **personal assistant** deployment: one trusted operator boundary, potentially many agents.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:53:- If someone can modify Gateway host state/config (`~/.openclaw`, including `openclaw.json`), treat them as a trusted operator.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:54:- Running one Gateway for multiple mutually untrusted/adversarial operators is **not a recommended setup**.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:60:### Practical consequence (operator trust boundary)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:62:Inside one Gateway instance, authenticated operator access is a trusted control-plane role, not a per-user tenant role.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:66:- Example: expecting per-operator isolation for methods like `sessions.list`, `sessions.preview`, or `chat.history` is outside this model.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:72:OpenClaw is designed as a personal assistant security model: one trusted operator boundary, potentially many agents.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:100:Treat Gateway and node as one operator trust domain, with different roles:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:102:- **Gateway** is the control plane and policy surface (`gateway.auth`, tool policy, routing).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:104:- A caller authenticated to the Gateway is trusted at Gateway scope. After pairing, node actions are trusted operator actions on that node.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:106:- Exec approvals (allowlist + ask) are guardrails for operator intent, not hostile multi-tenant isolation.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:120:| `canvas.eval` / browser evaluate            | Intentional operator capability when enabled      | \"Any JS eval primitive is automatically a vuln in this trust model\"           |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:121:| Local TUI `!` shell                         | Explicit operator-triggered local execution       | \"Local shell convenience command is remote injection\"                         |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:130:- Claims that classify normal operator read-path access (for example `sessions.list`/`sessions.preview`/`chat.history`) as IDOR in a shared-gateway setup.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:144:6. Deployment assumptions are explicit (loopback/local vs exposed, trusted vs untrusted operators).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:192:- **Policy drift/misconfig** (sandbox docker settings configured but sandbox mode off; ineffective `gateway.nodes.denyCommands` patterns because matching is exact command-name only (for example `system.run`) and does not inspect shell text; dangerous `gateway.nodes.allowCommands` entries; global `tools.profile=\"minimal\"` overridden by per-agent profiles; extension plugin tools reachable under permissive tool policy).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:217:1. **Anything “open” + tools enabled**: lock down DMs/groups first (pairing/allowlists), then tighten tool policy/sandboxing.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:219:3. **Browser control remote exposure**: treat it like operator access (tailnet-only, pair nodes deliberately, avoid public exposure).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:231:| `fs.config.perms_writable`                         | critical      | Others can change auth/tool policy/config                                            | filesystem perms on `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`                                                   | yes      |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:233:| `gateway.bind_no_auth`                             | critical      | Remote bind without shared secret                                                    | `gateway.bind`, `gateway.auth.*`                                                                  | no       |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:243:| `gateway.real_ip_fallback_enabled`                 | warn/critical | Trusting `X-Real-IP` fallback can enable source-IP spoofing via proxy misconfig      | `gateway.allowRealIpFallback`, `gateway.trustedProxies`                                           | no       |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:244:| `discovery.mdns_full_mode`                         | warn/critical | mDNS full mode advertises `cliPath`/`sshPort` metadata on local network              | `discovery.mdns.mode`, `gateway.bind`                                                             | no       |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:261:| `models.small_params`                              | critical/info | Small models + unsafe tool surfaces raise injection risk                             | model choice + sandbox/tool policy                                                                | no       |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:321:If you run the Gateway behind a reverse proxy (nginx, Caddy, Traefik, etc.), you should configure `gateway.trustedProxies` for proper client IP detection.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:323:When the Gateway detects proxy headers from an address that is **not** in `trustedProxies`, it will **not** treat connections as local clients. If gateway auth is disabled, those connections are rejected. This prevents authentication bypass where proxied connections would otherwise appear to come from localhost and receive automatic trust.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:327:  trustedProxies:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:337:When `trustedProxies` is configured, the Gateway uses `X-Forwarded-For` to determine the client IP. `X-Real-IP` is ignored by default unless `gateway.allowRealIpFallback: true` is explicitly set.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:358:- `gateway.controlUi.dangerouslyAllowHostHeaderOriginFallback=true` enables Host-header origin fallback mode; treat it as a dangerous operator-selected policy.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:359:- Treat DNS rebinding and proxy-host header behavior as deployment hardening concerns; keep `trustedProxies` tight and avoid exposing the gateway directly to the public internet.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:419:`/exec` is a session-only convenience for authorized operators. It does **not** write config or\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:519:Even with strong system prompts, **prompt injection is not solved**. System prompt guardrails are soft guidance only; hard enforcement comes from tool policy, exec approvals, sandboxing, and channel allowlists (and operators can disable these by design). What helps in practice:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:553:- Weak model tiers increase this risk. For hook-driven automation, prefer strong modern model tiers and keep tool policy tight (`tools.profile: \"messaging\"` or stricter), plus sandboxing where possible.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:632:- `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"` (default): only local clients can connect.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:800:- Gateway HTTP bearer auth is effectively all-or-nothing operator access.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:801:- Treat credentials that can call `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/responses`, `/tools/invoke`, or `/api/channels/*` as full-access operator secrets for that gateway.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:815:- If you terminate TLS in front of the Gateway, set `gateway.trustedProxies` to your proxy IPs.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:992:- For remote gateways, assume “browser control” is equivalent to “operator access” to whatever that profile can reach.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:1000:OpenClaw’s browser network policy defaults to the trusted-operator model: private/internal destinations are allowed unless you explicitly disable them.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:1024:With multi-agent routing, each agent can have its own sandbox + tool policy:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:1146:2. **Close exposure:** set `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"` (or disable Tailscale Funnel/Serve) until you understand what happened.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/security/index.md:1159:3. Review recent config changes (anything that could have widened access: `gateway.bind`, `gateway.auth`, dm/group policies, `tools.elevated`, plugin changes).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/tools-invoke-http-api.md:5:  - Building automations that need tool policy enforcement\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/tools-invoke-http-api.md:11:OpenClaw’s Gateway exposes a simple HTTP endpoint for invoking a single tool directly. It is always enabled, but gated by Gateway auth and tool policy.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/remote.md:12:- For **operators (you / the macOS app)**: SSH tunneling is the universal fallback.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/remote.md:29:- **Best UX:** keep `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"` and use **Tailscale Serve** for the Control UI.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/remote.md:151:- Treat browser control like operator access: tailnet-only + deliberate node pairing.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/index.md:83:| Bind mode    | CLI/override → `gateway.bind` → `loopback`                    |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/index.md:202:## Protocol quick reference (operator view)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:48:      \"mode\": \"operator\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:50:    \"role\": \"operator\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:51:    \"scopes\": [\"operator.read\", \"operator.write\"],\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:86:    \"role\": \"operator\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:87:    \"scopes\": [\"operator.read\", \"operator.write\"]\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:139:- `operator` = control plane client (CLI/UI/automation).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:142:### Scopes (operator)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:146:- `operator.read`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:147:- `operator.write`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:148:- `operator.admin`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:149:- `operator.approvals`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:150:- `operator.pairing`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:154:`/config set` and `/config unset` writes require `operator.admin`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:170:  even when it connects as both **operator** and **node**.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:179:- Operators may call `tools.catalog` (`operator.read`) to fetch the runtime tool catalog for an\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:188:- Operator clients resolve by calling `exec.approval.resolve` (requires `operator.approvals` scope).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:208:  `device.token.revoke` (requires `operator.pairing` scope).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:214:  - If that retry fails, clients should stop automatic reconnect loops and surface operator action guidance.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/protocol.md:225:- All WS clients must include `device` identity during `connect` (operator + node).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:34:3. OpenClaw checks that the request came from a **trusted proxy IP** (configured in `gateway.trustedProxies`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:48:- Keep gateway ingress locked to trusted proxy IPs only (`gateway.trustedProxies` + firewall).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:59:    trustedProxies: [\"10.0.0.1\", \"172.17.0.1\"],\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:78:If `gateway.bind` is `loopback`, include a loopback proxy address in\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:79:`gateway.trustedProxies` (`127.0.0.1`, `::1`, or an equivalent loopback CIDR).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:85:| `gateway.trustedProxies`                    | Yes      | Array of proxy IP addresses to trust. Requests from other IPs are rejected. |\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:147:    trustedProxies: [\"10.0.0.1\"], // Pomerium's IP\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:181:    trustedProxies: [\"127.0.0.1\"], // Caddy's IP (if on same host)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:213:    trustedProxies: [\"10.0.0.1\"], // nginx/oauth2-proxy IP\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:245:    trustedProxies: [\"172.17.0.1\"], // Traefik container IP\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:261:- [ ] **trustedProxies is minimal**: Only your actual proxy IPs, not entire subnets\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:272:- Missing `trustedProxies` configuration\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md:280:The request didn't come from an IP in `gateway.trustedProxies`. Check:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/troubleshooting.md:333:openclaw config get gateway.bind\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/nodes/index.md:12:A **node** is a companion device (macOS/iOS/Android/headless) that connects to the Gateway **WebSocket** (same port as operators) with `role: \"node\"` and exposes a command surface (e.g. `canvas.*`, `camera.*`, `device.*`, `notifications.*`, `system.*`) via `node.invoke`. Protocol details: [Gateway protocol](/gateway/protocol).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/nodes/index.md:76:If the Gateway binds to loopback (`gateway.bind=loopback`, default in local mode),\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/wizard.md:145:  --gateway-bind loopback \\\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/reference/RELEASING.md:16:When the operator says “release”, immediately do this preflight (no extra questions unless blocked):\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:27:  --gateway-bind loopback \\\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:61:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:71:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:81:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:93:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:103:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:113:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:123:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:133:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:145:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:159:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard-cli-automation.md:177:      --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/wizard.md:70:   Security note: if this agent will run tools or process webhook/hooks content, prefer the strongest latest-generation model available and keep tool policy strict. Weaker/older tiers are easier to prompt-inject.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/onboarding.md:35:- By default, OpenClaw is a personal agent: one trusted operator boundary.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/start/onboarding.md:38:- If hooks/webhooks or other untrusted content feeds are enabled, use a strong modern model tier and keep strict tool policy/sandboxing.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/diffs.md:285:- If gateway bind mode is `custom` and `gateway.customBindHost` is set, that host is used.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/diffs.md:352:  - use `gateway.bind=custom` and `gateway.customBindHost`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:15:Exec approvals are **in addition** to tool policy and elevated gating (unless elevated is set to `full`, which skips approvals).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:30:- Gateway-authenticated callers are trusted operators for that Gateway.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:31:- Paired nodes extend that trusted operator capability onto the node host.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:139:- It is intended for trusted operator environments where Gateway and node are in the same trust boundary.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:259:When a prompt is required, the gateway broadcasts `exec.approval.requested` to operator clients.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:281:  allowlist/full workflow where the operator accepts the broader runtime semantics.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:348:- if no operator UI or configured approval client can accept the request, the prompt falls back to `askFallback`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:392:- `/exec security=full` is a session-level convenience for authorized operators and skips approvals by design.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/exec-approvals.md:393:  To hard-block host exec, set approvals security to `deny` or deny the `exec` tool via tool policy.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/chrome-extension.md:163:Then ensure the tool isn’t denied by tool policy, and (if needed) call `browser` with `target=\"host\"`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:213:3. **Global tool policy** (`tools.allow` / `tools.deny`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:214:4. **Provider tool policy** (`tools.byProvider[provider].allow/deny`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:215:5. **Agent-specific tool policy** (`agents.list[].tools.allow/deny`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:217:7. **Sandbox tool policy** (`tools.sandbox.tools` or `agents.list[].tools.sandbox.tools`)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/multi-agent-sandbox-tools.md:218:8. **Subagent tool policy** (`tools.subagents.tools`, if applicable)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/subagents.md:5:  - You are changing sessions_spawn or sub-agent tool policy\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/elevated.md:29:- **Tool policy still applies**: if `exec` is denied by tool policy, elevated cannot be used.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/acp-agents.md:18:## Fast operator flow\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/acp-agents.md:245:- `label` (optional): operator-facing label used in session/banner text.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/acp-agents.md:331:Use `/acp spawn` for explicit operator control from chat when needed.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/index.md:82:## Provider-specific tool policy\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/context.md:34:Values vary by model, provider, tool policy, and what’s in your workspace.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/multi-agent.md:450:and a tighter tool policy:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/system-prompt.md:33:Safety guardrails in the system prompt are advisory. They guide model behavior but do not enforce policy. Use tool policy, exec approvals, sandboxing, and channel allowlists for hard enforcement; operators can disable these by design.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/presence.md:18:provide quick operator visibility.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/architecture.md:95:- All WS clients (operators + nodes) include a **device identity** on `connect`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/concepts/agent.md:52:subject to tool policy. `apply_patch` is optional and gated by\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/bonjour.md:83:- 在 `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` 中设置 `gateway.bind: \"tailnet\"`。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/bonjour.md:166:- `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` 中的 `gateway.bind` 控制 Gateway 网关绑定模式。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/configuration.md:2917:- `gateway.trustedProxies`：在 Gateway 网关前面终止 TLS 的反向代理 IP 列表。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/tailscale.md:99:- `gateway.bind: \"tailnet\"` 是直接 Tailnet 绑定（无 HTTPS，无 Serve/Funnel）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/tailscale.md:100:- `gateway.bind: \"auto\"` 优先 loopback；如果你想要仅 Tailnet，使用 `tailnet`。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/discovery.md:29:- **Gateway 网关 WS（控制平面）**：默认在 `127.0.0.1:18789` 上的 WebSocket 端点；可通过 `gateway.bind` 绑定到 LAN/tailnet。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/discovery.md:81:- `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` 中的 `gateway.bind` 控制 Gateway 网关绑定模式。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:92:如果你在反向代理（nginx、Caddy、Traefik 等）后面运行 Gateway 网关，应该配置 `gateway.trustedProxies` 以正确检测客户端 IP。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:94:当 Gateway 网关从**不在** `trustedProxies` 中的地址检测到代理头（`X-Forwarded-For` 或 `X-Real-IP`）时，它将**不会**将连接视为本地客户端。如果禁用了 Gateway 网关认证，这些连接会被拒绝。这可以防止认证绕过，否则代理的连接会看起来来自 localhost 并获得自动信任。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:98:  trustedProxies:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:105:配置 `trustedProxies` 后，Gateway 网关将使用 `X-Forwarded-For` 头来确定真实客户端 IP 以进行本地客户端检测。确保你的代理覆盖（而不是追加）传入的 `X-Forwarded-For` 头以防止欺骗。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:326:- `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"`（默认）：只有本地客户端可以连接。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:427:- 如果你在 Gateway 网关前面终止 TLS，请将 `gateway.trustedProxies` 设置为你的代理 IP。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:702:2. **关闭暴露：** 设置 `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"`（或禁用 Tailscale Funnel/Serve）直到你了解发生了什么。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/security/index.md:715:3. 审查最近的配置更改（任何可能扩大访问权限的内容：`gateway.bind`、`gateway.auth`、私信/群组策略、`tools.elevated`、插件更改）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/remote.md:36:- **最佳用户体验：** 保持 `gateway.bind: \"loopback\"` 并使用 **Tailscale Serve** 作为控制 UI。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:52:      \"mode\": \"operator\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:54:    \"role\": \"operator\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:55:    \"scopes\": [\"operator.read\", \"operator.write\"],\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:90:    \"role\": \"operator\",\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:91:    \"scopes\": [\"operator.read\", \"operator.write\"]\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:143:- `operator` = 控制平面客户端（CLI/UI/自动化）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:146:### 作用域（operator）\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:150:- `operator.read`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:151:- `operator.write`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:152:- `operator.admin`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:153:- `operator.approvals`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:154:- `operator.pairing`\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:170:  即使它同时以 **operator** 和 **node** 身份连接。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:180:- 操作者客户端通过调用 `exec.approval.resolve` 来解决（需要 `operator.approvals` 作用域）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:197:- 设备令牌可以通过 `device.token.rotate` 和 `device.token.revoke` 轮换/撤销（需要 `operator.pairing` 作用域）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/protocol.md:206:- 所有 WS 客户端在 `connect` 期间必须包含 `device` 身份（operator + node）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/troubleshooting.md:235:- 你将 `gateway.bind` 设置为非本地回环模式（`lan`/`tailnet`/`custom`，或本地回环不可用时的 `auto`）但没有配置认证。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/troubleshooting.md:241:- 修复：在该机器上启动 Tailscale（或将 `gateway.bind` 改为 `loopback`/`lan`）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/nodes/index.md:73:如果 Gateway 网关绑定到 loopback（`gateway.bind=loopback`，本地模式下的默认值），\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/start/wizard.md:199:  --gateway-bind loopback \\\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/start/wizard.md:215:  --gateway-bind loopback\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/start/wizard.md:226:  --gateway-bind loopback","cwd":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773527871611}}
